  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146700",
      "title": "Updating State Based On Previous State",
      "lectureOrder": 80,
      "videoOrder": 75,
      "sourceHash": "b4d758e096c020009cab0731060a8a4f18a2fd3c05d771b195c5c79ace5d6511",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.21,
          "en": "And of course we can do this with functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.21,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "We can add a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 11.067,
          "en": "that's called the addFavoriteHandler() {} for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.81,
          "end": 17.203,
          "en": "and a function that we could call removeFavoriteHandler()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.35,
          "end": 20.95,
          "en": "and I will also add a helper function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.95,
          "end": 24.14,
          "en": "which I'll name itemIsFavoriteHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.14,
          "end": 27.68,
          "en": "That's a function which will later help us determine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.68,
          "end": 30.183,
          "en": "whether a given item is a favorite or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.64,
          "end": 33.96,
          "en": "Now in the addFavoriteHandler item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.96,
          "end": 38.15,
          "en": "I expect to get my favoriteMeetup as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.15,
          "end": 38.99,
          "en": "And then in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.99,
          "end": 42.81,
          "en": "I wanna set my user favorites to the old array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.81,
          "end": 45.57,
          "en": "plus this new item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.57,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "Now for this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 51.36,
          "en": "we could use userFavorites.concat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.36,
          "end": 53.532,
          "en": "and add the (favoriteMeetup);",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.532,
          "end": 57.32,
          "en": "Concat is like push but returns a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.32,
          "end": 61.4,
          "en": "and it's then this new array with that added Meetup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.4,
          "end": 63.403,
          "en": "which we set as our new state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.72,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "But there is a gotcha.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 68.16,
          "en": "We should not do it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.16,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "even though it's typically will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 73.37,
          "en": "When working with useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.37,
          "end": 77.382,
          "en": "it is worth knowing that React actually does not process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.382,
          "end": 79.57,
          "en": "state updates instantly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.57,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "but it schedules them behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 85.93,
          "en": "And it still then processes them very quickly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.93,
          "end": 88.053,
          "en": "but not instantly necessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.94,
          "end": 92.08,
          "en": "Now because of that, when you update your state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.08,
          "end": 97.05,
          "en": "and your state updates depends on the latest state snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 101.62,
          "en": "there is a scenario where the state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.62,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "does not really reflect the latest state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 108.463,
          "en": "because the last state update wasn't processed yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.75999999999999,
          "end": 114.75999999999999,
          "en": "And because that is the case, there is an alternative form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.97999999999999,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "of calling this state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "if you depend on that last state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "Instead of passing the new value as I did it a second ago,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "you should pass a function to the state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 136.22,
          "en": "And that function will be executed for you by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.22,
          "end": 138.53,
          "en": "That function will then automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.53,
          "end": 141.61,
          "en": "receive the previous state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.61,
          "end": 144.38,
          "en": "So the (prevUserFavorites) here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.38,
          "end": 147.02,
          "en": "and you should return the updated state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.02,
          "end": 148.923,
          "en": "So in this case, (prevUserFavorites) where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 154.823,
          "en": "we then concat the {favoriteMeetup}; we get as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 157.4,
          "en": "This will guarantee",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.4,
          "end": 160.51,
          "en": "that we always get the latest state snapshot here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.51,
          "end": 163.95,
          "en": "because React will execute these functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.95,
          "end": 166.55,
          "en": "which we pass through the state updating functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.55,
          "end": 168.63,
          "en": "in the correct order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.63,
          "end": 171.47,
          "en": "So now, we have a guaranteed that we definitely work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.47,
          "end": 174.1,
          "en": "on the latest state snapshot here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.1,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "and that's therefore the better way of updating your state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 182.8,
          "en": "if you depend on a previous version of that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.8,
          "end": 186.69,
          "en": "And that's now how we could add a favorite item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.69,
          "end": 189.12,
          "en": "Now in removeFavoriteHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.12,
          "end": 192.01,
          "en": "we probably can expect a {meetupId}",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.01,
          "end": 195.37,
          "en": "which identifies the meetup that should be removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.37,
          "end": 197.96,
          "en": "And then we can update userFavorites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.96,
          "end": 202.81,
          "en": "Again, with this state updating a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.81,
          "end": 205.57999999999998,
          "en": "where we get the prevUserFavorites",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.57999999999998,
          "end": 207.97,
          "en": "and return a new state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.97,
          "end": 212.63,
          "en": "because here again, we rely on that previous state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.63,
          "end": 217.12,
          "en": "And here we then wanna return prevUserFavorites.filter();",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.12,
          "end": 219.86,
          "en": "because filter returns a new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.86,
          "end": 222.57,
          "en": "where we can filter out items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.57,
          "end": 224.79,
          "en": "And I wanna filter out the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 227.69,
          "en": "where the meetupId matches this Id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.69,
          "end": 229.203,
          "en": "we're getting as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.16,
          "end": 232.19,
          "en": "Filter is a built in method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.19,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "which takes a function as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 237.39,
          "en": "which executes for every item in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.39,
          "end": 240.65,
          "en": "and we get that item as a parameter then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.65,
          "end": 242.67,
          "en": "and then we have to return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.67,
          "end": 244.21,
          "en": "if we wanna keep that item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.21,
          "end": 247.9,
          "en": "or false if we wanna get rid of it in that new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.9,
          "end": 249.29,
          "en": "which has returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.29,
          "end": 251.09,
          "en": "And here I wanna return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.09,
          "end": 256.09,
          "en": "if meetup.id !==meetupId I get as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.69,
          "end": 258.26,
          "en": "So, if it is equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.26,
          "end": 261.28,
          "en": "we return false here because of this check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.28,
          "end": 265.42,
          "en": "and that means we drop the item where the Id is equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.42,
          "end": 268.36,
          "en": "And that means that the returned array will be missing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.36,
          "end": 270.96,
          "en": "the item which has this meetupId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.96,
          "end": 272.68,
          "en": "which is exactly what we need here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.68,
          "end": 275.053,
          "en": "since we want to remove that item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 275.94,
          "end": 278.68,
          "en": "And in itemIsFavoriteHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.68,
          "end": 281.61,
          "en": "I just want to return a response here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 281.61,
          "end": 283.12,
          "en": "I return a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.12,
          "end": 285.54,
          "en": "and I want to check whether...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.54,
          "end": 290.54,
          "en": "Let's say an item with a given Id is part of our favorites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 293.22,
          "en": "And for this, we don't need to update any state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.22,
          "end": 295.17,
          "en": "It's just a helper function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.17,
          "end": 298.58,
          "en": "where I return userFavorites.some();",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.58,
          "end": 300.4,
          "en": "which is a nav built-in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.4,
          "end": 303.2,
          "en": "which exists in Vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.2,
          "end": 307.52,
          "en": "And some also wants a function as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.52,
          "end": 310.52,
          "en": "which executes for every item in this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.52,
          "end": 313.81,
          "en": "and this function should return true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.81,
          "end": 317.98,
          "en": "And if at least one of the items in the array returns true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.98,
          "end": 319.99,
          "en": "or false with that function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.99,
          "end": 323.93,
          "en": "some overall will return true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.93,
          "end": 325.48,
          "en": "And that allows us to find out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.48,
          "end": 330.46,
          "en": "if some item in this array matches our condition here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.46,
          "end": 334.90999999999997,
          "en": "And the condition is that some meetup.id is == meetupId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.90999999999997,
          "end": 336.90999999999997,
          "en": "we get as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.90999999999997,
          "end": 338.36,
          "en": "So we return true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.36,
          "end": 343.36,
          "en": "if we have a meetup with that Id in our user favorites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.44,
          "end": 348.44,
          "en": "Now we get these free functions for changing our context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.5,
          "end": 352.633,
          "en": "but at the moment these functions are never called anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
